cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "lemur: Life expectancy monitor upscaled in R"
abstract: >-
  lemur is an R package and Shiny application for scenario analysis of
  mortality. Given the cause-of-death distribution of a population, it
  answers what-if questions (what would life expectancy be if cardiovascular
  mortality fell by 50%?), recomputes the life table, shows the gains and
  losses at every age, and decomposes the change by age and cause of death.
  It runs on the bundled Global Burden of Disease 2023 estimates from IHME.
